### What is the Graph Valid Tree problem?

You are given n nodes (labelled 0 to n-1) and a list of undirected edges. The task is to determine whether these edges form a valid tree. A valid tree means the graph is fully connected (every node is reachable from every other) and contains no cycle.

In banking, this validates that an approval hierarchy has exactly one path between any two positions and no circular approval loops.

### Why is edge count plus connectivity sufficient?

The key mathematical fact is: a graph on n nodes is a tree if and only if it has exactly n-1 edges and is connected. With exactly n-1 edges, connectivity and acyclicity are equivalent. You do not need a separate cycle test.

- Fewer than n-1 edges: the graph cannot be connected.
- Exactly n-1 edges and connected: no cycle is possible (adding one edge would create a cycle).
- More than n-1 edges: at least one cycle must exist.

```java
package com.bank.service;

import java.util.*;

public class HierarchyValidator {

    public static boolean isValidTree(int n, int[][] edges) {
        // Step 1: edge count check
        if (edges.length != n - 1) return false;

        // Step 2: build adjacency list
        List<List<Integer>> adj = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) adj.add(new ArrayList<>());
        for (int[] edge : edges) {
            adj.get(edge[0]).add(edge[1]);
            adj.get(edge[1]).add(edge[0]);
        }

        // Step 3: BFS from node 0
        boolean[] visited = new boolean[n];
        Queue<Integer> queue = new LinkedList<>();
        queue.offer(0);
        visited[0] = true;
        int visitCount = 1;

        while (!queue.isEmpty()) {
            int node = queue.poll();
            for (int neighbour : adj.get(node)) {
                if (!visited[neighbour]) {
                    visited[neighbour] = true;
                    visitCount++;
                    queue.offer(neighbour);
                }
            }
        }
        return visitCount == n;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[][] edges = {{0, 1}, {0, 2}, {0, 3}, {1, 4}};
        System.out.println("Valid tree: " + isValidTree(5, edges));
    }
}
```

